SUMMARY:Media as Civic Infrastructure: Building the Culture and Communities
  We Need
LOCATION:Commonwealth Club World Affairs of California\, Toni Rembe Rock Au
 ditorium\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94105
URL:https://www.commonwealthclub.org/events/2026-12-01/media-civic-infrastr
 ucture-building-culture-and-communities-we-need
DESCRIPTION:What if we understood local media not simply as a source of new
 s and information\, but as essential civic infrastructure? At a moment whe
 n local journalism is shrinking\, public trust is eroding\, and communitie
 s are increasingly disconnected\, we need to rethink the role media plays 
 in the places we call home. A healthy civic life depends on more than info
 rmed residents. It depends on people feeling connected to one another\, se
 eing themselves and their communities represented\, having opportunities t
 o participate in public life\, and developing a shared sense of belonging 
 and possibility.\n\nInfo & tickets: https://www.commonwealthclub.org/event
 s/2026-12-01/media-civic-infrastructure-building-culture-and-communities-w
 e-need
END:VEVENT
