SUMMARY:Should Huckleberry Finn Be Banned from Our Schools — For Its Own 
 Good?
LOCATION:The Commonwealth Club of California\, Taube Family Auditorium\, Sa
 n Francisco\, CA\, 94105
URL:https://www.commonwealthclub.org/events/2026-12-16/should-huckleberry-f
 inn-be-banned-our-schools-its-own-good
DESCRIPTION:The Adventures of Huckleberry Finn has been in trouble almost f
 rom the moment Mark Twain published it\, first in Britain in 1884 and then
  in the United States in 1885. The original objections included Huck’s b
 ad behavior and socially subversive thinking\, but also the book’s bad g
 rammar and unconventional language.\n\nInfo & tickets: https://www.commonw
 ealthclub.org/events/2026-12-16/should-huckleberry-finn-be-banned-our-scho
 ols-its-own-good
END:VEVENT
