SUMMARY:Chinese Americans: The Most Litigious\, Civilly Disobedient America
 ns
LOCATION:The Commonwealth Club of California\, Toni Rembe Rock Auditorium\,
  San Francisco\, CA\, 94105
URL:https://www.commonwealthclub.org/events/2027-01-14/chinese-americans-mo
 st-litigious-civilly-disobedient-americans
DESCRIPTION:David Y. Lei\, born in Taiwan\, immigrated to the United States
  in 1956. He began his career as a social worker in San Francisco’s Chin
 atown in the late 1960s\, working with young people involved in Chinatown 
 gangs. In 1981\, he entered the business world\, exporting consumer produc
 ts to Mexico. He sold his business in 2003 and retired. Lei served as vice
  chair of the Asian Art Museum board and directed San Francisco’s Chines
 e New Year Parade from 1977 to 2006.\n\nInfo & tickets: https://www.common
 wealthclub.org/events/2027-01-14/chinese-americans-most-litigious-civilly-
 disobedient-americans
END:VEVENT
