SUMMARY:MythBusters’ Adam Savage on Finding Joy in Making Things
LOCATION:Commonwealth Club World Affairs of California\, Taube Family Audit
 orium\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94105
URL:https://www.commonwealthclub.org/events/2027-01-19/mythbusters-adam-sav
 age-finding-joy-making-things
DESCRIPTION:Former "MythBusters" co-host Adam Savage has been described as 
 “a master maker\,” “a nerd’s nerd\,” and “somebody who blows s
 tuff up.” In his 2020 book Every Tool’s a Hammer\, he writes: “There
  was something special in the marriage between the structure of my brain a
 nd what I could do with my hands. When I made stuff\, the world made sense
  to me. It felt like my superpower.” Savage first used that superpower i
 n the special effects industry\, working on films like Star Wars: Episode 
 I – The Phantom Menace\, Galaxy Quest\, and the Matrix sequels.\n\nInfo 
 & tickets: https://www.commonwealthclub.org/events/2027-01-19/mythbusters-
 adam-savage-finding-joy-making-things
END:VEVENT
