SUMMARY:'Where You Find Me' Film Screening and Q&A
LOCATION:Commonwealth Club World Affairs of California\, Taube Family Audit
 orium\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94105
URL:https://www.commonwealthclub.org/events/2027-01-21/where-you-find-me-fi
 lm-screening-and-qa
DESCRIPTION:Where You Find Me is a short film directed by Jen Tocquigny tha
 t follows Betty Ann Bruno's journey working as a Munchkin in The Wizard of
  Oz to finding her way back to her family’s roots. After her family move
 d away from Hollywood\, her path was marked by many pivotal moments that s
 haped her career. Betty Ann took a job in the CIA\, went through a period 
 of civic activism in Oakland\, then an eventual run for City Council. She 
 went on to become a three-time Emmy Award-winning KTVU reporter—one of t
 he first broadcast positions for Asian-American women.\n\nInfo & tickets: 
 https://www.commonwealthclub.org/events/2027-01-21/where-you-find-me-film-
 screening-and-qa
END:VEVENT
