SUMMARY:NPR’s Emily Feng on How China’s Repression Fueled a Militant Mo
 vement…In Syria
LOCATION:Commonwealth Club World Affairs of California\, Toni Rembe Rock Au
 ditorium\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94105
URL:https://www.commonwealthclub.org/events/2027-01-26/nprs-emily-feng-how-
 chinas-repression-fueled-militant-movementin-syria
DESCRIPTION:What drove a few thousand men and women from the deserts and ci
 ties of western China to the front lines of Syria’s war? In her new book
 \, Our Hearts Burned for Home\, journalist Emily Feng unearths the untold 
 story of Uyghur exiles who fled China’s expanding police state—only to
  become a pivotal force behind the fall of Bashar al-Assad’s regime. At 
 the heart of this narrative is a startling paradox: Beijing’s repression
 \, meant to crush dissent\, instead scattered and radicalized a generation
 .\n\nInfo & tickets: https://www.commonwealthclub.org/events/2027-01-26/np
 rs-emily-feng-how-chinas-repression-fueled-militant-movementin-syria
END:VEVENT
