SUMMARY:Humanities West Presents Beethoven the Revolutionary
LOCATION:The Commonwealth Club of California\, Taube Family Auditorium\, Sa
 n Francisco\, CA\, 94105
URL:https://www.commonwealthclub.org/events/2027-03-26/humanities-west-pres
 ents-beethoven-revolutionary
DESCRIPTION:Ludwig van Beethoven died on March 26\, 1827\, after a lifetime
  of composing music that still thrills audiences around the world. Humanit
 ies West celebrates those invaluable cultural contributions on the 200th A
 nniversary of his death by featuring two Bay Area music scholars and popul
 ar lecturers—and a special focus on the Ode to Joy of Beethoven's Ninth 
 Symphony. The Road to the Ninth: Beethoven’s Symphonic Journey\n\nInfo &
  tickets: https://www.commonwealthclub.org/events/2027-03-26/humanities-we
 st-presents-beethoven-revolutionary
END:VEVENT
